# The fixes to step 28 from the review of its close, the engine's part:
# the cap of threads left running counted from when a thread is told to
# stop and looked at where a call starts, the system's name lookups held
# to a count until they return, every alternative of a manifest glob's
# braces relative to the workspace, and two rules of the host calls that
# no test held (a URL's user part, the bytes of the waiting host calls).

[break] a-thread-being-stopped-is-not-waited-for
rule: A start or a call of an extension waits while a thread of that extension is being stopped (in its grace), and is refused if that thread is left running.
file: crates/cineris-ext/src/engine/mod.rs
in: must_wait
find: if stopping.iter().any(|watched| watched.hash == *hash) {
replace: if false {
