caught-by:
    cineris-ext::it left_running::a_runtime_started_in_anothers_grace_waits_and_is_refused_when_that_one_is_left
    cineris-ext::it left_running::calls_of_other_sessions_made_in_a_grace_are_refused_once_that_thread_is_left

[break] a-thread-told-to-stop-is-not-counted
rule: A runtime's thread counts toward the cap from when it is told to stop, until it ends or is left running.
file: crates/cineris-ext/src/engine/mod.rs
in: ScriptRuntime::stop_thread
find: self.watched.tell();
replace: let _ = &self.watched;
packages: cineris-ext
caught-by:
    cineris-ext::it left_running::a_runtime_started_in_anothers_grace_waits_and_is_refused_when_that_one_is_left
    cineris-ext::it left_running::a_thread_whose_call_was_given_up_is_judged_by_the_next_start

[break] a-start-given-up-is-not-counted
rule: A start given up before its end tells its thread to stop, and the thread counts toward the cap until it ends or is left running.
file: crates/cineris-ext/src/engine/mod.rs
in: Starting::drop
find: watched.tell();
replace: let _ = watched;
packages: cineris-ext
caught-by:
    cineris-ext::it left_running::a_thread_whose_start_was_given_up_is_judged_by_the_next_start

[break] the-cap-is-not-looked-at-for-a-call
rule: Past the cap of threads left running, a runtime alive before the cap was reached takes no call.
file: crates/cineris-ext/src/engine/mod.rs
in: ScriptRuntime::call_to_its_end
find: if abandoned >= MAX_ABANDONED {
replace: if false {
packages: cineris-ext
caught-by:
    cineris-ext::it left_running::past_the_cap_a_runtime_alive_before_it_takes_no_call

[break] a-lookup-given-up-frees-its-place
rule: A system lookup holds its place among the process's lookups until the blocking lookup returns, not until its future is dropped.
file: crates/cineris-llm/src/fetch.rs
in: on_the_pool
find: let _place = place;
replace: drop(place);
packages: cineris-llm
caught-by:
    cineris-llm fetch::tests::a_lookup_given_up_holds_its_place_until_the_lookup_returns

[break] a-glob-is-looked-at-whole-not-by-its-alternatives
rule: Every alternative a manifest glob's braces give is relative to the workspace, nested braces included.
file: crates/cineris-ext/src/manifest.rs
in: check_glob
find: .all(|alternative| is_relative_glob(alternative))
replace: .all(|_| is_relative_glob(glob))
packages: cineris-ext
caught-by:
    cineris-ext::it manifest::no_alternative_of_a_globs_braces_leaves_the_workspace

[break] a-path-outside-the-workspace-matches-a-glob
rule: A path that leads outside the workspace is outside every manifest glob, one whose braces hold that very path among them included.
file: crates/cineris-ext/src/capability.rs
in: Capabilities::check
find: let inside = path.is_inside_workspace() && path.abs().starts_with(&self.workspace);
replace: let inside = true;
packages: cineris-ext
caught-by:
    cineris-ext::it capability::a_glob_whose_braces_name_a_path_outside_reads_nothing_there

[break] a-url-with-a-user-and-password-is-read
rule: A fetch's URL that names a user, or a user and a password, is refused before the manifest is asked.
